Various legal frameworks and international treaties within European human rights law address the issue of unequal treatment based on personal characteristics through a combination of directives, conventions, and judicial interpretations. Key among these are the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR) and the Council Directive 76/207/EEC, which focuses on the principle of equal treatment for men and women in employment and related areas.

